use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../Link import Link

export ui-component TableOfContents:
    description:
        A table of contents lists links to the headings on a long page, such
        as the sections of a help article. It follows the user as they scroll,
        showing which section they are reading.

    composes:
        - @{Link}

    items:
        Each item links to one heading on the page and knows that heading's
        level, so that lower-level headings can be indented under the ones
        above them. The component supplies the headings; whether the chosen
        library can also find them on the page by itself is up to it. The list
        has a name of its own, such as "On this page".

    tracking:
        As the user scrolls, the items for the headings in view are marked as
        active, both on screen and for assistive tools. More than one can be
        active at once, such as when several short sections fit on screen.
        What counts as in view, such as how far down the screen a heading must
        reach, is up to the chosen library, and the component can adjust it.

    following:
        Following an item scrolls the page to its heading and updates the
        page's address, so the user can share a link to that section. The next
        press of Tab carries on from that heading, not from the table of
        contents.

    scrollContainer:
        By default it follows the scrolling of the whole page. The component
        can point it at a scrolling panel instead, when the content scrolls
        inside one.

    keepingInView:
        If the table of contents is too long for its space and scrolls on its
        own, it scrolls itself to keep the active item in view. It never
        scrolls the page to do so. The component can turn this off.

    reporting:
        The component is told which headings are active whenever that changes,
        and can mark items active itself.

    nonGoals:
        - Not the site's main navigation. That's a NavigationMenu
        - Doesn't number headings or change the page's content
        - Doesn't collapse or expand sections of the list
